--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: aafc23d87a364a340bc9853e8f8116b9, type: 3}
  m_Name: JournalEntryBank
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entries:
  - id: Candle
    content: "In the realm of dreams, time itself seems to stand still, and evil
      does not dare set foot within it. Reality is the opposite \u2014 there, every
      passing moment works against me. If I wish to remain safe, I must remember
      what allowed me to fall asleep.\r\n\r\nThis chamber is no ordinary prison.
      I can feel that it hides secrets whose discovery may weaken the bonds of the
      curse. If I unravel every mystery hidden within these walls, perhaps I will
      find a way out."
  - id: Rock
    content: The pile of spinning wheels has fallen silent. Let the light of the
      candle return darkness to it. To reduce the painted wood to ashes, you must
      cast upon it an illusion of flames shaped from shadow and light.
  - id: FirePlace
    content: 'Follow the path carved by fate: from that which still breathes with
      life, to that which bears authority, and finally to that which remains after
      life has departed. Keep a proper distance between them, for even in dreams
      they should never meet.'
  - id: Cage
    content: The two worlds breathe in opposite, mirrored rhythms. What remains trapped
      in reality demands to be locked away within the dream. The symbol carved into
      the unyielding metal of the waking world will reveal what you must seek on
      the other side of the mirror.
  - id: Raven
    content: The witch's feathered messenger has abandoned the place where it belonged.
      As long as its black wings obscure the light, the truth will remain hidden.
      Return it to the place where it kept watch from the very beginning, and the
      light shall dispel the shadow.
  - id: Timelock
    content: "When the princess fell into a deep sleep, two faithful attendants kept
      watch by her bedside. On the first night, they waited for a miracle, but zero
      came. They saw no signs from fate, so they dared to leave the chamber. Then
      three ravens perched at the window and watched over the princess\u2019s sleep
      for eternity."
